WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.450
A honey bee lands back at the hive
and starts to dance on the comb.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.960
Other bees crowd round and follow it.

3
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:11.400
Then they fly out and head for a patch
of flowers they've never visited.

4
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.780
Something has been passed on.

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.750
But is that language?

6
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.770
In this mission, you'll find out
why animals communicate at all:

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.810
for survival, reproduction,
territory and food.

8
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.320
You'll decode the dance: how the angle
of the waggle run points the way,

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:33.160
using the sun as a guide, and how
its length shows how far the food is.

10
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.760
Then you'll see what
human language can do,

11
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.930
like planning next week's party.

12
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: decide whether the
bee dance really counts as language.
